=== the arc the records come from: the time seat's, end to end ===
arc: the time seat's arc matched its pin, and left the till's record at two moments, with the statements beside it
clock: every roll is called at a moment derived from the statements' own times; what is pinned is how long ago
=== A: the first roll, over the record the till published at its third boot ===
A: roll: fleet nuage -- 2 members, 1 keeps a record; as of <time>, by the caller's clock
A: roll: dates come from clockbox (fingerprint FP1): an entry "existed no later than" a time, which is that member's word and never a lower bound
A: roll: this is the first roll: there is nothing to compare it with
A: roll: clockbox -- keeps no record: its machine declares no JOURNAL, so there is none to bring
A: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
A: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
A: roll: 1 of 1 record held
A: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, and is its member's, in order from its first entry
A: roll: written to zig-out/roll/a.roll: the next roll is compared with it (--since)
A: exit 0
=== B: two hours later, over the record it published at its fifth boot, against A ===
B: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 2 h 5 min before this one by the caller's clock
B: roll: till -- 4 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
B: roll: till -- entry 3 of 4 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word); the entry after it is ORDERED and UNDATED
B: roll: till -- WROTE 2 entries since the roll of <time> (entries 3-4); the first existed no later than <time>, and the last one is ORDERED and UNDATED
B: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 1 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
B: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, is its member's, and goes on from the roll before it wherever that roll held it
B: roll: written to zig-out/roll/b.roll: the next roll is compared with it (--since)
B: exit 0
=== C: the same record again, against B ===
C: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
C: roll: till -- 4 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
C: roll: till -- entry 3 of 4 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word); the entry after it is ORDERED and UNDATED
C: roll: till -- NOTHING NEW since the roll of <time>: the record brought still ends at entry 4, head H8
C: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 1 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
C: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, is its member's, and goes on from the roll before it wherever that roll held it
C: exit 0
=== D: nobody brings the record, against B ===
D: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
D: roll: till -- ABSENT: its machine keeps a record at /data/journal, and none was brought
D: roll: till -- the roll of <time> held it: 4 entries, head H8, newest dated entry 3 no later than <time>
D: roll: 0 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 1 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
D: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
D: roll: written to zig-out/roll/d.roll: the next roll is compared with it (--since)
D: exit 1
=== D2: the record comes back, against D ===
D2: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 1 h 30 min before this one by the caller's clock
D2: roll: till -- 4 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
D2: roll: till -- entry 3 of 4 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word); the entry after it is ORDERED and UNDATED
D2: roll: till -- NOTHING NEW since the roll of <time>: the record brought still ends at entry 4, head H8
D2: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 1 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
D2: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, is its member's, and goes on from the roll before it wherever that roll held it
D2: exit 0
=== E: the record as it stood before B, against B: shorter than B saw ===
E: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
E: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
E: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
E: roll: till -- DIVERGED: the roll of <time> held 4 entries and this record holds 2: a record is only ever extended, so this one was cut back, is another device's, or is not the one that roll saw. It stays DIVERGED until a roll is called again without --since
E: roll: 0 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 0 absent, 1 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
E: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
E: roll: written to zig-out/roll/e.roll: the next roll is compared with it (--since)
E: exit 1
