E3: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 1 h 30 min before this one by the caller's clock
E3: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
E3: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
E3: roll: till -- DIVERGED: the roll of <time> held 4 entries and this record holds 2: a record is only ever extended, so this one was cut back, is another device's, or is not the one that roll saw. It stays DIVERGED until a roll is called again without --since
E3: roll: 0 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 0 absent, 1 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
E3: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
E3: exit 1
=== E4: the short record, with no roll before it ===
E4: roll: this is the first roll: there is nothing to compare it with
E4: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
E4: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
E4: roll: 1 of 1 record held
E4: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, and is its member's, in order from its first entry
