=== E5: the short record, against E4 ===
E5: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 1 h before this one by the caller's clock
E5: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
E5: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
E5: roll: till -- NOTHING NEW since the roll of <time>: the record brought still ends at entry 2, head H8
E5: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 1 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
E5: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, is its member's, and goes on from the roll before it wherever that roll held it
E5: exit 0
=== F: an entry taken out of the middle of the record, against B ===
F: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
F: roll: till -- BROKEN at entry 3: the entry is not the one this place holds (seq=<its place> prev=...): an entry was removed, reordered or replaced, or these are not an entry's bytes; 2 entries verified before it
F: roll: till -- the break is inside what the roll of <time> vouched for (4 entries): entries that roll saw have been changed or removed
F: roll: 0 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
F: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
F: exit 1
=== G: one second added to a statement, against B ===
G: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
G: roll: till -- 4 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
G: roll: till -- entry 3 of 4 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word); the entry after it is ORDERED and UNDATED
G: roll: till -- FINDING: 1 of 3 statements did not verify against clockbox's key and it is not taken: changed after it was signed, signed by another, cut short, or not a statement
G: roll: till -- NOTHING NEW since the roll of <time>: the record brought still ends at entry 4, head H8
G: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 1 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
G: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
G: exit 1
=== H: the record cut at its end, with the authority's statements about what was cut, against B ===
H: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
H: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
H: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
H: roll: till -- FINDING: 1 statement verifies and is about entries this record does not hold: it is another record's, or entries were cut from the end of this one
H: roll: till -- DIVERGED: the roll of <time> held 4 entries and this record holds 2: a record is only ever extended, so this one was cut back, is another device's, or is not the one that roll saw. It stays DIVERGED until a roll is called again without --since
H: roll: 0 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 0 absent, 1 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
H: roll: NOT clean: 2 things the set owes an answer for
H: exit 1
=== I: the fleet before the till's key was enrolled ===
I: roll: this is the first roll: there is nothing to compare it with
I: roll: till -- NOT ENROLLED: the fleet holds no key for it, so nobody can speak for its records until its own fingerprint is enrolled
I: roll: 0 of 1 record held
I: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
I: roll: not written (no --out): nothing was kept, so the next roll will be a first roll too
I: exit 1
=== M: a roll shown a record older than the authority's own date for an entry ===
M0: roll: this is the first roll: there is nothing to compare it with
M0: roll: till -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
M0: roll: till -- entry 2 of 2 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word)
M0: roll: 1 of 1 record held
M0: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, and is its member's, in order from its first entry
M0: roll: written to zig-out/roll/m0.roll: the next roll is compared with it (--since)
M0: exit 0
M: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 2 h 5 min before this one by the caller's clock
M: roll: till -- 4 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
M: roll: till -- entry 3 of 4 existed no later than <time> (clockbox's word); the entry after it is ORDERED and UNDATED
M: roll: till -- WROTE 2 entries since the roll of <time> (entries 3-4); the first existed no later than <time>, and the last one is ORDERED and UNDATED
M: roll: till -- FINDING: the authority dates the first of them no later than <time>, which is before the roll of <time>, the roll that did not have it: the copy that roll was shown was stale, or the caller's clock and the authority's disagree
M: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 1 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
M: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
M: exit 1
=== O: the record brought with no statements beside it, against B ===
O: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, 3 h 35 min before this one by the caller's clock
O: roll: till -- 4 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H8, and no secret took part
O: roll: till -- every entry is ORDERED and UNDATED here: no statements were brought beside the record
O: roll: till -- NOTHING NEW since the roll of <time>: the record brought still ends at entry 4, head H8
O: roll: 1 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 1 had nothing new, 0 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
O: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, is its member's, and goes on from the roll before it wherever that roll held it
O: exit 0
=== J: the roll is a file, and the same call twice writes the same bytes ===
file: B and J are the same 268 bytes
file: A: roll v1 fleet=nuage at=A authority=FP
file: A: member clockbox state=none entries=0 head=- dated=0 t=- last=-
file: A: member till state=held entries=2 head=H dated=2 t=BOUND2 last=A
file: A: end
file: B: roll v1 fleet=nuage at=B authority=FP
file: B: member clockbox state=none entries=0 head=- dated=0 t=- last=-
file: B: member till state=held entries=4 head=H dated=3 t=BOUND3 last=B
file: B: end
file: D: roll v1 fleet=nuage at=C authority=FP
file: D: member clockbox state=none entries=0 head=- dated=0 t=- last=-
file: D: member till state=absent entries=4 head=H dated=3 t=BOUND3 last=B
file: D: end
file: E: roll v1 fleet=nuage at=C authority=FP
file: E: member clockbox state=none entries=0 head=- dated=0 t=- last=-
file: E: member till state=diverged entries=4 head=H dated=3 t=BOUND3 last=B
file: E: end
file: E4: roll v1 fleet=nuage at=E4 authority=FP
file: E4: member clockbox state=none entries=0 head=- dated=0 t=- last=-
file: E4: member till state=held entries=2 head=H dated=2 t=BOUND2 last=E4
file: E4: end
=== K: what is refused, in words ===
K1: harb: roll takes a fleet file and the directory the records were brought to: harb roll <file.fleet> <dir> [--since <roll>] [--at <time>] [--out <roll>]
K1: exit 1
K2: harb: roll: --at is seconds since the epoch or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MMZ, not 'yesterday'
K2: exit 1
K3: harb: cannot read zig-out/roll/none.roll: there is no such roll
K3: exit 1
K4: harb: zig-out/roll/junk.roll is not a roll: it is a file `harb roll --out` writes, in the one spelling it reads back
K4: exit 1
K5: harb: zig-out/roll/other.roll is a roll of fleet elsewhere, and this is fleet nuage: the anchors in it are another fleet's
K5: exit 1
K6: harb: cannot open zig-out/roll/nowhere, the directory the records were brought to: FileNotFound
K6: exit 1
K7: roll: compared with the roll of <time>, which the caller's clock reads as LATER than this one: the two are not one clock's
K7: roll: till -- ABSENT: its machine keeps a record at /data/journal, and none was brought
K7: roll: till -- the roll of <time> held it: 4 entries, head H8, newest dated entry 3 no later than <time>
K7: roll: 0 of 1 record held; since the last roll 0 wrote, 0 had nothing new, 1 absent, 0 diverged, 0 new, 0 left the fleet
K7: roll: NOT clean: 1 thing the set owes an answer for
K7: harb: roll: nothing was written: this roll is as of a time earlier than the roll it was compared with, and a roll file is kept only in the order of the caller's clock -- call it with a later --at, or with no --since to start again
K7: exit 1
file: K7 wrote no roll
